  "correctionToL3385": "L3385 stated that the registry's anti-repair rows are not the Repair Tool's damage to vehicles. Nothing stored supports that; what 'AntiRepair Amount Per Second' applies to is not read."
 },
 "inference": [
  "Stacking table: counts 2 to 8 with multipliers 0.75, 0.58, 0.5, 0.4, 0.33, 0.28, 0.25. Count times multiplier is 1.5, 1.74, then 2 from four upward, which fits a per-source multiplier that caps the combined repair of several repairers at about twice one repairer. The field names are hashes, so 'number of simultaneous repairers' is a candidate reading.",
  "The registry gives repair as 40 per second (60 with the active-repair upgrade; 30 and 60 in Battle Royale) on a 0.1 s apply interval, and 'AntiRepair' as 30 per second (45 with the upgrade; 15 and 30 in Battle Royale). Whether 'AntiRepair' is the damage dealt to enemy vehicles, or something else, is not read.",
  "Damage entries 10, 5, 7.5, 12.5, 15, 17.5, 20 and heal entries 2.5 to 20 are rank tables. The registry's 'Damage Vehicle Rank' 3 and 5 point at 12.5 and 17.5 if the rank is the entry index (candidate, joined by name). No heal rank row was found, and no heal entry equals 40 or 60 times 0.1, so the per-second rows and the entries are different quantities or one of them is unused.",
  "Eight entries of Affector_VehicleRepair carry no table and 0 in Field_9f3374a0; the others carry 1 and, in all but one, 0.8 in Field_0528bc34. What distinguishes the 16 entries is not read.",
  "Grid for the tool's material 479: 1 against tanks and IFVs, 1.25 against helicopters, 2 against light vehicles."
 ],
 "unresolved": [
  "Repair rate with one and with two repairers on the same tank (40 per second and 60 combined expected if the table is per repairer).",
  "Repair Tool damage per second against an enemy tank (30 if 'AntiRepair' is that damage; 125 if entry 3 applies every 0.1 s)."
 ],
